### 3\. NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURE DECISION

### 3.1 One canonical content publication system

The authoritative content entity is:

```text
posts/{postId}
```

Every social video publication must have exactly one canonical publication identity.

A video published through Create Post and distributed in Sparks must not become two separate publications.

The same publication must be discoverable through the relevant Arvdoul surfaces:

* Home.

* Sparks.

* Following.

* Friends.

* Explore.

* Search.

* Creator profiles.

* Saved content.

* Notifications.

* Shared links.

* Analytics.

* Sponsored distribution.

* Paid promotion.

The same `postId` must identify that publication across all these surfaces.

The canonical post owns:

* Author identity.

* Caption and description.

* Publication type.

* Audience and visibility.

* Publication status.

* Hashtags and topics.

* Location.

* Creation and publication timestamps.

* Scheduling metadata.

* Content permissions.

* Publication lifecycle.

* Moderation status.

* Distribution eligibility.

* Post-level engagement summary.

* Relevant monetization configuration.

* Relationships to attached media.

Do not create a second social publication under `videos/{videoId}` for the same video.

### 3.2 Separate content ownership from media ownership

A media asset is not a social publication.

Keep the domains separate:

Canonical publication — `posts/{postId}`

One author, caption, audience, publication lifecycle, distribution identity and engagement ownership

Canonical media asset

One media asset identity and authoritative processing state, linked to its publicationMux asset ID · playback ID · duration · thumbnail · renditions · processing status

Sparks

Video discovery and playback

Other surfaces

Home, profiles, search and sharing

Inspect the existing media-storage abstraction before deciding where media asset records belong.

Reuse an existing suitable media entity where possible. If the current `videos` collection must be transformed to own only media-asset information, do so safely and document that ownership boundary.

Do not create another media system merely because it has a different name.

A media asset must not independently own the social publication's comments, likes, followers, author identity, visibility or distribution ranking.

The canonical post references its media assets. Media processing updates the asset's authoritative state and communicates the appropriate publication-state transition.

